            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MommyFromSeattle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been making this for a solid 5 years and has been a hit everytime! But I always add something green, usually chopped green onions and place 4-5 stalk on top befor baking to make it visually appealing. You can also add chopped can chiles or diced pimentos (in a jar) for great color. And using low fat sour cream tastes exactly the same too. But after 5 years, and using 3 different ovens, this dish always takes about 50-55 min. to bake, not 45 min. Can also make ahead and refridgerate before you need to bake, just let it sit at room temperature for at least 30-45 min. Great for making ahead for a dinner party. Be sure to print out recipes because you will get asked!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "IRISHMAIDEN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this casserole for Thanksgiving the last two years. There is never a crumb left! Everyone loves it. I make it with only 3 TBSP melted butter and 1 egg, plus 1/2 cup chopped onion. This makes it lighter and more savory. I bake it at 350 for 1 hour. Another plus to this recipe is when I make it for Thanksgiving I double it and put it in my 9x13 Pyrex portable glass pan with a microwaveable warmer. I make it earlier, then bring a great side dish that doesn't require valuable oven space!",
            "datePublished": "2003-07-22T09:07:01.513Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "POCHICKA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is definitely on the top of the list of requests for dinner sides. I have made it full fat and reduced fat and still have the same great response! I use a 1/2 cup of egg beaters, reduced fat sour cream and margarine (instead of butter). Bake at 375 for an hour and 15 minutes; it turns out beautifully. LOVE THIS ONE!!",
            "datePublished": "2006-10-30T05:57:23.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kelliegirl21"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I LOVED THIS RECIPE!! and so did everyone of our guests! Not one drop was left! I would just add a bit less butter...I used a clean dish towel to absorb the excess oil from the butter on top when it was done. added grated cheddar cheese, chopped red bell pepper cause they are sweeter than the green ones..Other wise, leave the recipe like it is ! Thanks Ruthie, you done yourself good! Happy Memorial Day , Yes ! Because of this casserole! IT is now a favorite of ours!~",
            "datePublished": "2003-05-26T21:54:43.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RACHAEL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made this several times now, its definately a family favorite. I LOVE this. The second time I made it, I was out of sour cream and didnt know it so I substituted with mayonnaise and it turned out delicious. My family prefers the mayo version, which is slightly sweeter and my Mom and Dad make the sour cream version which is a little tangy. Both ways are sooo good. Highly recommend this one.",
            "datePublished": "2003-03-21T18:37:53.000Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FizzyThyme7420"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is just like the corn casserole my mom used to make. To add some interest I chopped up 2 jalapeños and a bunch of green onions and added them in. I melted the butter (I actually used about 6 tablespoons instead of the full half cup) in my cast iron skillet and then cooked the casserole in the cast iron. And lastly, I grated some Parmesan cheese on top before baking which created a beautiful crisp top.",
            "datePublished": "2023-10-11T23:07:15.338Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cher"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The base of this recipe is very good. However, I added a small can of diced green chilies and 1/3 cup of Sargentos 4 cheddar shredded cheese. It is a huge hit at all gatherings with an added kick.",
            "datePublished": "2023-03-11T02:55:24.596Z"
          },
          {
